title: Payers › Workflow Builder › Build from scratch
route: /payers/summit?tab=builder
intro: A blank workflow has a Start and an End, apart, and nothing between them. It cannot be published until the steps are added and connected, and the checks say so.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Click 'Blank' (New menu)\nor 'Build from scratch' (empty state)"
overlay o1 "Right-hand panel 'Build from scratch'\n'You get a Start and an End. Add steps from the list on the left of the canvas and connect them.'"
input i1 "Optionally name it, pick a service and request type"
click c1 "Click 'Create the draft'"
store st1 "Workflow saved as a draft with Start and End only\nVersion history first line: 'Started from a blank canvas'"
screen s2 "Canvas with two steps and no lines\nSettings panel 'This workflow'"
process p1 "Checks list two problems, each with 'Go to node'\n'Nothing follows Start' and 'End cannot be reached from Start'"
click c2 "Click 'Publish' now"
toast t1 "'Cannot publish yet: 2 things need fixing.'"
click c3 "Add steps and connect them"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Workflow Builder › Add, move and connect steps"
end e1 "A blank draft is open and ready to build"

s1 --> o1 --> i1 --> c1 --> st1 --> s2 --> p1 --> e1
p1 --> c2 --> t1
t1 --> c3
s2 --> c3 --> g1
